condition_name: Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)
condition_slug: hepatocellular-carcinoma-hcc
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "The most common primary liver malignancy. HCC has a huge burden on West Africa due to the high endemicity of a number of risk factors like hepatitis B, C, and HIV. In Nigeria, middle aged individuals, mainly males, are more commonly affected and they present late."
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Elective
    features[5]: Painful right hypochondrial mass,weight loss,early satiety,fatigue,ascites
  - type: Emergency
    features[3]: Coagulopathy,encephalopathy,acute abdomen (rupture and haemorrhage)
investigations[8]: Liver biopsy,Abdominopelvic USS,Abdominal CT,LFT,Serum proteins,"Electrolyte, Urea and Creatinine","Tumour markers (α-fetoprotein, des-gamma-carboxy prothrombin, C-reactive protein)",FBC
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[0]:
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[3]: Hepatitis B screening and vaccination,Abdominal USS/CT,"Serological markers: α-fetoprotein"
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[6]: "Liver resection - early stages, solitary lesions",arterial ligation for non-resectable lesions,Systemic chemotherapy,percutaneous ethanol injection,radiotherapy,radiofrequency ablation
prognosis: null